meta {
  name: Optimize
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/analytics/portfolio/optimize
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "objective": "RISK_PARITY",
    "constraints": {
      "max_weight": 0.35,
      "allow_shorts": false
    },
    "risk_aversion": 3.0
  }
}

docs {
  Objectives: MIN_VARIANCE, MEAN_VARIANCE, MAX_SHARPE, RISK_PARITY, EQUAL_WEIGHT, INVERSE_VOL.

  Expected returns default to the Black-Litterman equilibrium (reverse-optimised from market-cap
  weights) rather than to sample means, which are far too noisy to feed an optimiser. Override
  with "expected_returns": {"NVDA": 0.15, ...}.

  RISK_PARITY returns near-identical riskContributions; if the box constraint binds, the message
  says so, because equal contribution is then unreachable.
}
